FerrionOS change to base (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 20f7573b4dc011ea5267189185edc0b2f12bab0f, applied after ferrion-sigchld.patch:
Check the sender's credentials for signals sent through process and group handles.
- a signal sent through a process handle (proc-obj) or a process group handle (pgrp-obj) names the process that made the call as its sender, so kill()'s permission check and the sender information use that process's credentials.
- a signal sent through a group handle fails, like kill() on a group, when no member of the group could be signalled.

